Description: connect an Ubuntu desktop to Microsoft Entra ID with authd
 Sesame connects an Ubuntu Desktop 24.04 or newer to Microsoft Entra ID
 through authd and its authd-msentraid snap, then lets the Entra account
 take over the existing local account: same UID, same home directory, same
 groups, same crontab.
 .
 Every step detects whether it is already done and can be run again. A
 backup is made before each step that changes something, a rescue
 administrator account can be created, and the takeover is rolled back
 automatically if it fails (or by hand with "sesame annuler-reprise"). It
 is best done at the next boot, by a systemd service that runs before any
 session.
 .
 It comes as a graphical assistant ("sesame-assistant", GTK 4 and
 libadwaita, which needs the recommended packages), a command line
 ("sesame") and a root helper launched through pkexec. The Entra
 application must be created in the Entra portal; Sesame explains how.
 .
 The package installs a signed APT repository entry, so "apt upgrade" keeps
 Sesame up to date.

